<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_CrossLinkAdjacent" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.9.0">
  <bpmn:process id="Process_CrossLinkAdjacent" name="Cross-linked chain continuation" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Rule L7 fixture: when a NON-SPINE chain walk reaches a split it continues
into the successor whose subtree carries a forward flow into already-chained
territory, in preference to the first-declared one.

Shape: the spine is Start -&gt; Prepare -&gt; Ready to ship -&gt; End. A secondary start
runs Receive -&gt; Sort -&gt; G_Route, and G_Route splits two ways:

  declared 1st: Bundle -&gt; Pack -&gt; End_Shipped   (no link back)
  declared 2nd: Reconcile                        (links back to Ready to ship)

Reconcile is the cross-linked successor: it carries Flow_H_I into Ready to ship,
which the spine already claimed. First-declared and cross-linked therefore
disagree, which is the whole point of the fixture — the declaration order
puts Bundle first on purpose.

Continuing into Bundle stranded Reconcile one tier further down, and its
cross link into Ready to ship then had no corridor and was routed around the far
left margin of the diagram. Continuing into Reconcile keeps it on the row
its rejoin needs, and the cross link becomes a short elbow.

Exercises:
  - Reconcile shares a row with Sort (it continues that chain),
  - Bundle sits strictly below that row (it became the branch),
  - the cross link is at most three waypoints and never leaves the
    diagram's left edge.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_A" name="Order placed">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_A_B</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_A_B" sourceRef="Start_A" targetRef="Task_B" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_B" name="Prepare order">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_A_B</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_B_I</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_B_I" sourceRef="Task_B" targetRef="Task_I" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_I" name="Ready to ship">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_B_I</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_H_I</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_I_D</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_I_D" sourceRef="Task_I" targetRef="End_D" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_D" name="Order shipped">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_I_D</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_E" name="Returns arrived">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_E_F</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_E_F" sourceRef="Start_E" targetRef="Task_F" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_F" name="Sort returns">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_E_F</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_F_G</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_F_G" sourceRef="Task_F" targetRef="G_G" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="G_G" name="Restock?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_F_G</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_G_L</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_G_H</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_G_L" name="scrap" sourceRef="G_G" targetRef="Task_L" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_L" name="Bundle for scrap">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_G_L</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L_J</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L_J" sourceRef="Task_L" targetRef="Task_J" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_J" name="Pack pallet">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L_J</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_H_J</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_J_K</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_J_K" sourceRef="Task_J" targetRef="End_K" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_K" name="Pallet shipped">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_J_K</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_G_H" name="restock" sourceRef="G_G" targetRef="Task_H" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_H" name="Reconcile stock">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_G_H</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_H_I</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_H_J</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_H_I" sourceRef="Task_H" targetRef="Task_I" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_H_J" sourceRef="Task_H" targetRef="Task_J" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_CrossLinkAdjacent">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_CrossLinkAdjacent" bpmnElement="Process_CrossLinkAdjacent" />
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
